<article class="env-lemma" id="07VZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07VZ">Lemma <span data-tag="07VZ">81.6.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ A \ar[r] \ar[d] &  C \ar[d] \ar[r] &  E \ar[d] \\  B \ar[r] &  D \ar[r] &  F }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume that $A, B, C, D$ and $A, B, E, F$ form cartesian squares and that $B \to D$ is surjective étale. Then $C, D, E, F$ is a cartesian square. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is formal. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>